\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Best passive gain per cell of the $(\lVert \bm  {k}\rVert ,\lvert D\rvert )$ plane (light grey: cell without energy). Left: modelled in-vivo residuals (STI and off-diagonal terms plus noise, RC1): the gain depends on $\lvert D\rvert $ and hardly on $\lVert \bm  {k}\rVert $. Middle: white noise on RC1: the gain depends on $\lVert \bm  {k}\rVert $ (about 1 below $0.1$ cycles/voxel, falling to $\lesssim 0.1$ above $0.4$ for $\lvert D\rvert <0.1$) and weakly on $\lvert D\rvert $. Right: the noise-like $\psi $ of the real Sim2.}}{3}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gains}{{1}{3}{Best passive gain per cell of the $(\norm \bk ,\abs D)$ plane (light grey: cell without energy). Left: modelled in-vivo residuals (STI and off-diagonal terms plus noise, RC1): the gain depends on $\abs D$ and hardly on $\norm \bk $. Middle: white noise on RC1: the gain depends on $\norm \bk $ (about 1 below $0.1$ cycles/voxel, falling to $\lesssim 0.1$ above $0.4$ for $\abs D<0.1$) and weakly on $\abs D$. Right: the noise-like $\psi $ of the real Sim2}{figure.caption.10}{}}
\newlabel{fig:gains@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][3][]3}{}{}{}}
